  "severity": {
    "cvss_v3_score": 8.8,
    "rating": "critical"
  },
  "source_feeds": [
    "nvd"
  ],
  "summary": "Out-of-bounds write (CWE-787) in the lossless (VP8L) decoder of libwebp 1.3.1, the September 2023 zero-day. While decoding the per-image Huffman descriptors, the decoder builds a lookup structure into a fixed-capacity buffer sized for a balanced code, including a 128-entry on-stack array used when reading the code-length descriptors. A maliciously crafted image can supply a valid but deeply unbalanced set of code lengths whose secondary lookup levels need more entries than the buffer holds, so the builder writes entries past the end of that buffer, corrupting adjacent stack or heap memory. This is reachable from any caller that decodes an attacker-supplied WebP image, and was exploited as a zero-day in the wild. Affects libwebp 1.3.1."
}

